  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {放|ほう} (to release) and {屁|ひ} (gas/flatulence). This is the formal, medical, or literary term. In everyday conversation, おなら is overwhelmingly more common. {放屁|ほうひ} appears mainly in medical contexts, formal writing, or humorous elevated speech.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {放屁|ほうひ}する: to pass gas (formal)\n- {頻繁|ひんぱん}な{放屁|ほうひ}: frequent flatulence\n- {放屁|ほうひ}の{回数|かいすう}: number of times passing gas\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- おなら: fart — the standard everyday word\n- {屁|へ}: fart — informal, slightly vulgar\n- ガス: gas — euphemistic medical term (as in お{腹|なか}にガスが{溜|た}まる)",
